          { name: "Demographic Invisibility of Smaller Communities and Minority Constituencies", tag: "avoid", why: "MN-SD-8's demographic profile is overwhelmingly white (86.99%), with Black (2.61%), Hispanic (2.54%), Asian (1.81%), and unaccounted (~6.05%, likely including multiracial and other categories) populations that together represent roughly 13% of the district. While small in proportion, these communities have specific economic and social concerns — workplace equity, immigration policy, educational opportunity, and healthcare access — that can become invisible in a politics centered entirely on white renter and homeowner economics. Any candidate who governs this district as though the 87% white majority encompasses the entire constituency is systematically neglecting nearly one in eight residents and leaving a credibility gap that opposition mobilization could exploit." }
