          { name: "Framing the District as Monolithic Anglo Republican Suburb", tag: "avoid", why: "MN-SD-28 is 91.12% white with negligible Hispanic (2.8%) and Asian (1.82%) populations, but the 4.6% gap in the demographic categories likely represents American Indian constituents whose specific concerns — particularly around tribal sovereignty, gaming revenue, and state-tribal relations — are often absent from Republican campaign messaging in majority-white suburban districts. Ignoring or minimizing these communities' presence, even at small percentages, signals that the representative does not serve the actual district and can create openings for opposition mobilization among constituencies that feel overlooked." }
