          "Build specific equity outcomes, not diversity rhetoric, with the Black (11.29%), Asian (8.82%), and Hispanic (6.64%) communities: measurable progress on educational attainment gaps, healthcare access in underserved neighborhoods, and representation in local boards and hiring is what moves these constituencies beyond baseline support.",
          "Address housing affordability and rental-market stability for the 30.2% renter population: younger professionals and dual-income households in a $104,596 median-income district are managing real housing-cost pressures that require concrete policy—zoning reform, development incentives, or rental-market regulation—depending on local context.",
          "Do not attempt to broaden the coalition by moderating on core Democratic priorities (climate, education funding, equity): the 63% margin reflects alignment on these issues, not tolerance for watering them down—challenge and growth come from executing better on what the constituency already wants, not repositioning toward Republican voters who have other options."
