          { name: "Overlooking the College-Educated Swing Voter", tag: "avoid", why: "The 43.4% college-educated plurality is the swing demographic in SD-55—these voters evaluate on competence, policy specificity, and results rather than party loyalty. Any candidate who campaigns to the party base without specifically engaging college-educated voters on education outcomes, fiscal management, and whether government is solving problems loses the primary constituency that decides close races in affluent, educated districts. In a 55-45 race, the college-educated swing voter is not a secondary audience; they are the central audience." }
