          "Engage the renter minority (28.2%) with specific housing and affordability policy: while homeowners dominate SD-55 by count, renters include younger professionals and service workers whose economic mobility depends on housing affordability, property tax fairness, and whether wages are keeping pace with cost of living. Ignoring this constituency in a district this narrow is a strategic error.",
          "Do not treat 55% as a stable floor: in a district where median income is $97,183 and college attainment is 43.4%, a 55-45 partisan margin indicates a genuinely swing constituency evaluating on competence and results, not inherited loyalty. Either party's candidate who assumes the existing coalition will hold without active engagement of the educated homeowner majority and the economic concerns of younger professionals will find the margin narrower than expected.",
          "Address tax burden and return on public investment directly: high-income constituencies in affluent Minnesota districts are acutely aware of their tax burden and evaluate whether they are receiving corresponding value. The incumbent must defend specific programs and outcomes; the challenger must make a compelling case that resources are being misallocated or that current governance is inefficient."
