          { name: "Framing as a Suburban 'Culture War' District", tag: "avoid", why: "MN-SD-56's demographic profile — highly educated, affluent, professionally oriented, 37.8-year median age — is not compatible with a campaign built around abstract cultural grievances or divisive social issues. Voters in this district evaluate candidates on competence, specific policy knowledge, and whether the candidate understands their material economic concerns. A campaign that defaults to culture-war positioning in a district where 48.5% are college-educated and $110,071 is median income will be perceived as intellectually unserous and will perform worse than the generic Republican position. This district demands specific, sophisticated policy engagement, not ideological theater." }
