          { name: "Treating a 71% Margin as Permanent Rather Than a Product of Sustained Service", tag: "avoid", why: "A 71-29 result is commanding, but in a district with no meaningful demographic diversity and a relatively stable age and income profile, it reflects alignment between the incumbent's record and the base's interests — not inherited loyalty or an uncontestable position. Any incumbent who campaigns this seat as though the 71% is a permanent floor, who becomes inattentive to constituent concerns, or who prioritizes partisan positioning over local problem-solving risks creating an opening for a credible challenger who offers better constituent service. This margin is real, but it requires active maintenance through concrete delivery on the issues that matter to older homeowners in northern Minnesota." }
