          { name: "Assuming AIAN Communities Are Either Absent or Irrelevant to Representation", tag: "avoid", why: "The 4.7% demographic gap cannot be written off as measurement error or incidental population; in Minnesota, with its documented tribal presence and treaty framework, unaccounted-for AIAN residents represent actual constituents with governance expectations. A representative who systematically ignores this population—or assumes their voting behavior without genuine engagement—is not fully representing the district and is creating a vulnerability if tribal political organization increases. Minnesota's state-level relationship with tribal nations makes this a governance obligation, not an optional outreach priority." }
