          "Engage the 6.6% demographic gap as a constituent relationship, not a footnote: this likely represents American Indian residents with distinct governance expectations around resource access, tribal consultation, and local economic development; active partnership with tribal leadership and indigenous constituents builds durability in a seat that appears safe but requires ongoing legitimacy work.",
          "Lead with constituent service infrastructure: the 29.1% college attainment and practical homeowner focus suggest a constituency that evaluates representatives on direct problem-solving — constituent casework responsiveness, property tax appeals support, and local service delivery are more electorally powerful than ideological positioning.",
          "Monitor the renter minority (19.5%) and younger household formation: while homeowners dominate this district, the one-in-five renter households and above-average median age signal a constituency with limited younger adult anchoring; if economic opportunity or housing affordability deteriorates significantly, demographic drift toward Democratic support becomes possible in a state with this political trajectory."
