          "Engage regional economic development with specificity to Brainerd and North-Central Lakes: the 25.8% college-educated rate slightly below state average suggests that education-to-employment pipeline and regional job quality are the underlying economic concerns. A representative who speaks fluently to manufacturing competitiveness, healthcare sector development, and workforce retention commands credibility.",
          "Address exurban service delivery as a material constituent priority: broadband access, emergency services response times, and road maintenance in low-density areas are the friction points where homeowner dissatisfaction originates. These are not glamorous issues but they are the daily experience of governance for the 84% homeowner majority.",
          "Do not assume the 30% opposition is fixed: in a district this demographically Republican, the 30% represents dissatisfaction within the base rather than partisan conversion. Understanding whether it is driven by incumbent performance gaps, a strong challenger, or localized grievances is essential to holding the seat or expanding the margin."
