          { name: "Dismissing Hispanic Community Needs as Separate from Core Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "At 8% of the population, Hispanic residents are not a marginal constituency—they are integrated into the district's agricultural and food-processing workforce and part of the core economic functioning of west-central Minnesota communities like Willmar. A candidate whose messaging treats Hispanic community concerns (language access, economic mobility, immigration status stability for workforce participation) as distinct from or competing with the interests of white homeowners will fail to recognize that these communities' economic fates are genuinely interdependent in districts built on agricultural and processing-sector employment." }
