          "Monitor the 44% Republican base for intensity and organization — in a 56-44 seat, a motivated Republican minority plus modest Democratic turnout decline produces a competitive race; identify whether opposition is concentrated among a specific demographic or geographic subset and address defections before they compound in lower-turnout cycles."
