          { name: "Positioning the Renter Constituency as Non-Stakeholders", tag: "avoid", why: "Any framing that treats renters as a separate or temporary constituency rather than as stakeholders building economic stability and wealth in HD-26A will underperform among the 33.9% of the district that rents. Renters at $65,865 household income are not economically marginal — they are the working-age professionals and families whose housing costs, childcare needs, and wage growth directly determine their political alignment. Messaging that ignores renter economic concerns or treats homeowner priorities as the district's only legitimate priorities will cede this constituency to any challenger who offers a credible alternative." }
