          "Engage the AIAN constituency (5.6% of population) with institutional respect and specific governance knowledge — Indian Health Service access, tribal consultation in land-use decisions, and economic partnership are the issues that matter to this community, and active engagement prevents latent opposition from mobilizing.",
          "Monitor the 14.2% renter population as a potential swing constituency in the next cycle: younger renters in a heavily owner-occupied community may have different priorities around housing affordability and tenant protections, and they represent the only substantial demographic group not fully reflected in the current 74% result.",
          "Avoid treating 74% as a permanently safe margin: while the consolidation is strong, any legislator who neglects the renter and AIAN constituencies, or who fails to remain responsive to the blue-collar and small-business base on its specific economic priorities, creates an opening for a challenger with a more targeted engagement strategy."
