          { name: "Overlooking the Renter Minority (17.5%) as a Potential Organizing Target", tag: "avoid", why: "While renters represent only 17.5% of the district and are likely young, transient, or economically marginal within HD-28A's homeowner-dominant political economy, they represent a constituency whose economic concerns (housing affordability, wage stagnation, healthcare access) are unaddressed by a homeowner-focused legislative agenda. In a district where the incumbent holds a commanding margin, Democratic opposition has incentive to organize renters as a swing constituency if housing pressures intensify. Ignoring this community entirely creates a governance blind spot and a potential organizing vulnerability." }
