          { name: "School Quality and Funding", tag: "lean-into", why: "In a district where 52.1% of adults hold college degrees, median household income is $117,098, and 83.2% own their homes, school performance is a primary metric by which households evaluate their state representative's competence. Bahner's 55% win was conditional on the perception that Democratic governance delivers superior educational outcomes; any incumbent or challenger must demonstrate concrete evidence — test scores, graduation rates, per-pupil spending efficiency — that their approach to school funding produces results. A 5-10 point swing in parent satisfaction with school performance is sufficient to flip this seat." },
          { name: "Property Tax Management and Fiscal Discipline", tag: "lean-into", why: "With 83.2% homeownership and median income of $117,098, property holders in MN-HD-37B are acutely sensitive to whether their state representative is managing the tax burden responsibly. The 55% Democratic result reflects confidence that Democratic governance can fund schools and infrastructure without imposing unsustainable tax increases; if property tax rates rise perceptibly faster than income growth, the incumbent's margin erodes quickly. Fiscal stewardship — demonstrated through specific examples of cost control and efficient public spending — is the competence issue that separates winning from losing in this district." },
          { name: "Conservative Fiscal Governance Among Affluent Voters", tag: "careful", why: "The 45% Republican opposition in a 79.85% white, 52.1% college-educated, $117,098 median income district represents affluent, educated voters who believe Republican governance delivers superior fiscal outcomes. These voters are not motivated by cultural conservatism but by a substantive view that lower taxes and less regulation produce better economic outcomes; they are responsive to evidence-based arguments about tax efficiency and government waste. Any Democrat who dismisses this 45% as ideologically rigid rather than engaging it on its actual fiscal concerns will lose ground in a district where affluent, educated voters are persuadable based on competence." },
          { name: "Treating 55% as a Durable Partisan Floor", tag: "avoid", why: "The incumbent's margin reflects conditional support from voters who care about competent governance, not party loyalty. A representative who assumes the 55% is secure because MN-HD-37B is trending Democratic, or who becomes complacent about demonstrating ongoing results in schools and infrastructure, will find the margin eroding when a credible challenger offers a competing vision of fiscal stewardship. In affluent, educated suburban districts, partisan assumptions are dangerous; only demonstrated competence sustains electoral margins." },
          { name: "Partisan Ideology or Cultural Positioning", tag: "avoid", why: "MN-HD-37B voters are not responsive to culture-war framing or abstract partisan positioning. With 52.1% college attainment and $117,098 median income, this constituency evaluates candidates on concrete governance outcomes — school quality, tax fairness, infrastructure maintenance — not on whether they signal cultural identity or ideological purity. Any candidate who leads with partisan rhetoric rather than specific policy results on the issues that matter to affluent suburban homeowners will find their message bouncing off an audience that simply does not care about ideological positioning." }
