          "Lead on housing affordability and renter protection as a district priority — the 36.3% renter rate and $70,644 median income mean that housing cost burden is a direct squeeze on a substantial plurality of households, and visible legislative action on rent stabilization, tenant rights, and affordable development is a material service delivery issue, not abstract advocacy.",
          "Address educational opportunity and school performance explicitly for young families — the 32.5 median age and 27.9% college attainment suggest a constituency investing in their children's futures but concerned about whether public schools are delivering; school quality, safety, and equitable resources across neighborhoods are live issues that shape whether young families remain in or leave the district.",
          "Do not assume the 74% margin indicates reduced accountability for economic inclusion — in a young, multiracial, renter-heavy district, the incumbent's authority rests on demonstrable progress on housing, schools, and economic mobility, not on inherited Democratic loyalty; a challenger who articulates a more credible plan for these material concerns could move significant vote share even from a strong incumbent."
