          { name: "School Quality, Funding, and Educational Competence", tag: "lean-into", why: "At 61.6% college attainment and $122,037 median household income, HD-42B is a professional-class constituency whose families' educational stakes are direct and substantial. School funding adequacy, teacher quality, curriculum rigor, and the capacity of local schools to serve college-bound families are not abstract policy questions — they are the material foundation of family economic strategy. A representative who demonstrates sustained engagement with school boards, advocacy for adequate funding, and responsiveness to quality concerns is earning the trust that underlies the 64% margin." },
          { name: "Environmental Sustainability and Land-Use Competence", tag: "lean-into", why: "Affluent suburban constituencies at this income and education level consistently prioritize environmental quality, sustainable development, and the protection of green space and neighborhood character. The 29.8% renter rate and $122,037 median income together suggest homeowners with substantial property values whose long-term asset security is tied to environmental quality, water management, and land-use decisions. A representative who builds relationships with city planning processes and delivers on these environmental governance concerns is reinforcing the alignment between the constituency's material interests and Democratic governance." },
          { name: "Tax Efficiency and Public Sector Fiscal Management", tag: "careful", why: "While the 64-36 margin is substantial, affluent homeowners and professionals are consistently sensitive to questions about whether tax dollars are being spent efficiently and whether public sector costs are growing faster than acceptable. At this income level, property tax management and the perception of government waste are genuine constituent concerns that a 36% Republican opposition can activate if the incumbent appears indifferent to fiscal discipline. Demonstrating active engagement with municipal budgets and willingness to make efficiency arguments is necessary to prevent this constituency from becoming persuadable." },
          { name: "Partisan Activation and Base Mobilization Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "HD-42B's 64-36 Democratic margin is not built on partisan energy or base mobilization — it is built on sustained alignment between the incumbent's competence and the constituency's material interests in school quality, community stability, and professional quality of life. A campaign that relies on partisan activation, attacks on Republican voters as illegitimate, or ideological positioning risks alienating the educated, skeptical constituency that actually holds this seat by treating them as Democratic voters to be energized rather than affluent professionals to be served." },
          { name: "Dismissing or Rhetorical Defeat of Republican Concerns About Fiscal Responsibility", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district where 36% voted Republican and the remaining voters are educated professionals accustomed to skeptical evaluation of competing claims, any attempt to position fiscal responsibility concerns as illegitimate or to dismiss them through partisan framing will create an opening for a credible Republican challenger. This constituency wants to hear both parties' substantive arguments about how to deliver good schools and efficient government — not partisan theater. Failing to engage this legitimate constituency concern with seriousness and specificity is the primary vulnerability for the incumbent." }
