          { name: "Overlooking the 32.3% Renter Constituency as Distinct from Homeowner Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "The renter rate of 32.3% in a $93,546-income district represents a significant demographic block whose economic interests—rent stability, tenant protections, housing supply—diverge from homeowner property-value and tax concerns. An incumbent who positions housing policy primarily around tax relief and single-family zoning protection risks alienating the renter majority and creating an opening for opposition positioned as defending renter interests. This constituency requires clear differentiation between renter and homeowner housing policy rather than messaging that assumes homeowner priorities." }
