          "Recognize that 85% is not a perpetual mandate — it is a current alignment that depends on representation quality and local issue responsiveness; any incumbent or successor who treats the supermajority as sufficient reason to reduce constituent engagement or legislative visibility risks finding that turnout declines or a credible challenger emerges in the next cycle."
