          { name: "Neglecting the Absence of Republican Competition as a Meaningful Signal", tag: "avoid", why: "A 100% result with no Republican challenger listed may reflect weak right-wing institutional infrastructure in this urban district, voter demoralization on the right, or active strategic retreat from an unwinnable seat. Assuming that this represents permanent Democratic dominance rather than investigating why opposition has effectively conceded the terrain means missing early warning signals if those conditions shift. Understanding why the seat is 100% is analytically prior to treating the 100% as stable." }
