          "Maintain active engagement with the Black (14.3%) and Latino (6.79%) communities as distinct constituencies within the dominant coalition — demographic diversity within a 100% margin creates the risk that these communities' specific concerns become absorbed into generic Democratic messaging rather than addressed with targeted policy attention and constituent service.",
          "Use the uncontested status to build legislative infrastructure and reputation on issues that matter most to young renters and educated professionals: housing affordability and zoning reform, public transit investment, public safety and community policing, and neighborhood economic development that serves existing residents rather than displacing them.",
