          { name: "Assuming Demographic Diversity Automatically Produces Coalition Cohesion", tag: "avoid", why: "Demographic diversity is HD-65B's defining characteristic, but diversity alone does not guarantee a cohesive coalition—each community within the district has specific economic and social concerns that require dedicated constituent attention. Generic appeals to 'diversity' or 'inclusion' without concrete policy delivery on housing, wages, healthcare, and economic opportunity will appear hollow to communities of color evaluating on whether government is actually serving them. Any candidate who treats this district as though demographic diversity substitutes for specific constituent engagement will discover that assumption is wrong." }
